Wait for all pods to be ready:
oc get pods -w
Press Ctrl+C when all pods show STATUS as Running and READY as 1/1.

Subtask 1.3: Create Gateway Configuration
Now we'll create a Gateway resource to define how external traffic enters the mesh.

Create the Gateway configuration:
cat << 'EOF' > bookinfo-gateway.yaml
apiVersion: networking.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: Gateway
metadata:
  name: bookinfo-gateway
  namespace: bookinfo-ingress
spec:
  selector:
    istio: ingressgateway
  servers:
  - port:
      number: 80
      name: http
      protocol: HTTP
    hosts:
    - bookinfo.example.com
    - "*"
  - port:
      number: 443
      name: https
      protocol: HTTPS
    tls:
      mode: SIMPLE
      credentialName: bookinfo-credential
    hosts:
    - bookinfo.example.com
EOF

oc apply -f bookinfo-gateway.yaml
Verify the Gateway was created:
oc get gateway -n bookinfo-ingress
Subtask 1.4: Configure Virtual Service for Routing
Create a VirtualService to define routing rules for incoming traffic.

Create the VirtualService configuration:
cat << 'EOF' > bookinfo-virtualservice.yaml
apiVersion: networking.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: VirtualService
metadata:
  name: bookinfo-vs
  namespace: bookinfo-ingress
spec:
  hosts:
  - bookinfo.example.com
  - "*"
  gateways:
  - bookinfo-gateway
  http:
  - match:
    - uri:
        exact: /productpage
    - uri:
        prefix: /static
    - uri:
        exact: /login
    - uri:
        exact: /logout
    - uri:
        prefix: /api/v1/products
    route:
    - destination:
        host: productpage
        port:
          number: 9080
  - match:
    - uri:
        prefix: /health
    route:
    - destination:
        host: productpage
        port:
          number: 9080
    headers:
      response:
        add:
          x-custom-header: "health-check"
EOF

oc apply -f bookinfo-virtualservice.yaml
Verify the VirtualService was created:
oc get virtualservice -n bookinfo-ingress
Task 2: Test External Access to Services
Subtask 2.1: Get Ingress Gateway External Access Information
Get the ingress gateway external IP or hostname:
export INGRESS_HOST=$(oc get route -n istio-system istio-ingressgateway -o jsonpath='{.spec.host}')
echo "Ingress Host: $INGRESS_HOST"
Get the ingress gateway ports:
export INGRESS_PORT=$(oc get route -n istio-system istio-ingressgateway -o jsonpath='{.spec.port.targetPort}')
export SECURE_INGRESS_PORT=443
echo "HTTP Port: $INGRESS_PORT"
echo "HTTPS Port: $SECURE_INGRESS_PORT"
Set the gateway URL:
export GATEWAY_URL=$INGRESS_HOST:$INGRESS_PORT
echo "Gateway URL: $GATEWAY_URL"
Subtask 2.2: Test HTTP Access
Test basic connectivity to the productpage:
curl -I http://$GATEWAY_URL/productpage
Expected output should show HTTP 200 OK response.

Test the full productpage response:
curl -s http://$GATEWAY_URL/productpage | grep -o "<title>.*</title>"
Test API endpoints:
curl -s http://$GATEWAY_URL/api/v1/products | head -20
Test health endpoint with custom header:
curl -I http://$GATEWAY_URL/health
Look for the custom header x-custom-header: health-check in the response.

Subtask 2.3: Test Different Host Headers
Test with specific host header:
curl -H "Host: bookinfo.example.com" -I http://$GATEWAY_URL/productpage
Test with different host header (should still work due to wildcard):
curl -H "Host: test.example.com" -I http://$GATEWAY_URL/productpage
Subtask 2.4: Create Advanced Routing Rules
Let's create more sophisticated routing rules to demonstrate advanced ingress control.

Create a new version of the VirtualService with advanced routing:
cat << 'EOF' > bookinfo-advanced-vs.yaml
apiVersion: networking.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: VirtualService
metadata:
  name: bookinfo-advanced-vs
  namespace: bookinfo-ingress
spec:
  hosts:
  - bookinfo.example.com
  - "*"
  gateways:
  - bookinfo-gateway
  http:
  - match:
    - headers:
        user-agent:
          regex: ".*Mobile.*"
      uri:
        prefix: /
    route:
    - destination:
        host: productpage
        port:
          number: 9080
    headers:
      response:
        add:
          x-device-type: "mobile"
  - match:
    - uri:
        exact: /productpage
    - uri:
        prefix: /static
    - uri:
        exact: /login
    - uri:
        exact: /logout
    - uri:
        prefix: /api/v1/products
    route:
    - destination:
        host: productpage
        port:
          number: 9080
    timeout: 10s
    retries:
      attempts: 3
      perTryTimeout: 3s
  - match:
    - uri:
        prefix: /admin
    route:
    - destination:
        host: productpage
        port:
          number: 9080
    headers:
      request:
        add:
          x-admin-access: "true"
EOF

oc apply -f bookinfo-advanced-vs.yaml
Test mobile user agent routing:
curl -H "User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 14_0 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/14.0 Mobile/15E148 Safari/604.1" -I http://$GATEWAY_URL/productpage
Look for the x-device-type: mobile header in the response.

Test admin endpoint with custom header:
curl -H "x-admin-access: true" -I http://$GATEWAY_URL/admin
Task 3: Monitor Inbound Traffic and Policies
Subtask 3.1: Enable Traffic Monitoring
Check if Kiali is installed:
oc get pods -n istio-system -l app=kiali
Access Kiali dashboard (if available):
oc get route -n istio-system kiali
Generate traffic for monitoring:
for i in {1..50}; do
  curl -s http://$GATEWAY_URL/productpage > /dev/null
  echo "Request $i completed"
  sleep 1
done
Subtask 3.2: Monitor with Command Line Tools
Check ingress gateway logs:
oc logs -n istio-system -l app=istio-ingressgateway -f --tail=20
Run this in a separate terminal and generate traffic to see real-time logs.

Check proxy statistics:
INGRESS_POD=$(oc get pods -n istio-system -l app=istio-ingressgateway -o jsonpath='{.items[0].metadata.name}')
oc exec -n istio-system $INGRESS_POD -- curl -s localhost:15000/stats | grep -E "(inbound|outbound|upstream_rq)"
Check configuration dump:
oc exec -n istio-system $INGRESS_POD -- curl -s localhost:15000/config_dump | grep -A 10 -B 10 "bookinfo"
Subtask 3.3: Implement Security Policies
Create an Authorization Policy for the ingress gateway:
cat << 'EOF' > ingress-authz-policy.yaml
apiVersion: security.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: AuthorizationPolicy
metadata:
  name: ingress-policy
  namespace: bookinfo-ingress
spec:
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: productpage
  rules:
  - from:
    - source:
        principals: ["cluster.local/ns/istio-system/sa/istio-ingressgateway-service-account"]
  - to:
    - operation:
        methods: ["GET", "POST"]
        paths: ["/productpage", "/api/v1/products/*", "/static/*"]
  - when:
    - key: request.headers[user-agent]
      notValues: ["*bot*", "*crawler*"]
EOF

oc apply -f ingress-authz-policy.yaml
Test the authorization policy:
# This should work
curl -I http://$GATEWAY_URL/productpage

# This should be blocked
curl -H "User-Agent: GoogleBot/2.1" -I http://$GATEWAY_URL/productpage
Create a rate limiting policy:
cat << 'EOF' > rate-limit-policy.yaml
apiVersion: networking.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: EnvoyFilter
metadata:
  name: rate-limit-filter
  namespace: istio-system
spec:
  workloadSelector:
    labels:
      app: istio-ingressgateway
  configPatches:
  - applyTo: HTTP_FILTER
    match:
      context: GATEWAY
      listener:
        filterChain:
          filter:
            name: "envoy.filters.network.http_connection_manager"
    patch:
      operation: INSERT_BEFORE
      value:
        name: envoy.filters.http.local_ratelimit
        typed_config:
          "@type": type.googleapis.com/udpa.type.v1.TypedStruct
          type_url: type.googleapis.com/envoy.extensions.filters.http.local_ratelimit.v3.LocalRateLimit
          value:
            stat_prefix: http_local_rate_limiter
            token_bucket:
              max_tokens: 10
              tokens_per_fill: 10
              fill_interval: 60s
            filter_enabled:
              runtime_key: local_rate_limit_enabled
              default_value:
                numerator: 100
                denominator: HUNDRED
            filter_enforced:
              runtime_key: local_rate_limit_enforced
              default_value:
                numerator: 100
                denominator: HUNDRED
EOF

oc apply -f rate-limit-policy.yaml
Subtask 3.4: Test Rate Limiting
Generate rapid requests to test rate limiting:
for i in {1..15}; do
  echo "Request $i: $(curl -o /dev/null -s -w "%{http_code}" http://$GATEWAY_URL/productpage)"
done
You should see some requests return 429 (Too Many Requests) after the rate limit is exceeded.

Subtask 3.5: Monitor Security Events
Check for denied requests in logs:
oc logs -n istio-system -l app=istio-ingressgateway | grep -E "(403|429|RBAC)"
Monitor authorization policy effectiveness:
oc exec -n istio-system $INGRESS_POD -- curl -s localhost:15000/stats | grep rbac
Troubleshooting Tips
Common Issues and Solutions
Gateway not receiving traffic:

Check if the Gateway selector matches the ingress gateway labels
Verify the VirtualService is bound to the correct Gateway
Ensure the namespace labels are correct
503 Service Unavailable errors:

Verify that the destination service exists and is running
Check if the service selector matches the pod labels
Ensure sidecar injection is enabled
Certificate issues for HTTPS:

Create the TLS secret in the istio-system namespace
Verify certificate validity and format
Check Gateway TLS configuration
Rate limiting not working:

Verify EnvoyFilter is applied to the correct workload
Check Envoy proxy configuration dump
Monitor rate limiting statistics
Verification Commands
# Check all ingress-related resources
oc get gateway,virtualservice,authorizationpolicy -n bookinfo-ingress

# Verify ingress gateway configuration
istioctl proxy-config listeners $INGRESS_POD.istio-system

# Check virtual service configuration
istioctl proxy-config routes $INGRESS_POD.istio-system

# Verify authorization policies
istioctl proxy-config rbac $INGRESS_POD.istio-system
